ChildPatch: default-codex-home-for-local-processes

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Give Linux processes independent, ensured CODEX_HOME and CODEX_HARNESS roots and preserve the selected roots through configuration reload and embedded startup.

Requires: none

Provides: Default home to /codex and harness to /harness, canonicalize and publish both roots at startup, propagate them through Config and fixtures, and select protected harness/editor buffers with permission and symlink checks.

Boundary: Configuration and durable data remain in home; individual runtime consumers, project storage roots, and TMPDIR selection belong to their own responsibilities.

Verification: utils/home-dir tests, core config root tests, config_manager_preserves_the_selected_process_roots, startup_reloads_the_callers_selected_project, and external_editor buffer_tests verify defaults, propagation, independence, and protected placement.


